Subject: Stop the sums of error costs at the maximum of 32 bits

Stop the sums of the error costs at the maximum of 32 bits.

The copy of the runtime of the tree-sitter-cpp fork has this repair. The fork commit is
f8b702b.

ef148db gives a cost of 10000 to each unmatched right brace. It adds an
assertion that the cost of an ERROR node is at least the sum of these
costs in its ERROR children. The sums of the costs used 32 bits, and a
larger sum became smaller than its parts. At 2699626, error recovery at
an unterminated string added millions of MISSING tokens. A child of an
ERROR node then got a cost of 4,294,956,930. With the cost 10,601 of a
second child, the sum became 679, and the assertion stopped the parse.

The error costs of subtrees and of stack versions now stop at
ERROR_COST_MAX (UINT32_MAX). The sums use 64 bits before they stop, and
a sum with no part of ERROR_COST_MAX is exact. A part of ERROR_COST_MAX
gives that cost to the sum. The ERROR node invariant is then true for
each cost less than the maximum, and the assertion excludes the maximum.

With the previous loop of ts_parser__do_all_potential_reductions, the
parse of `b<C>(b<D>(e"x` and a `}` on the next line does not stop at the
assertion. It ends after 37.5 s with 7,040,930 MISSING nodes.

The tree hashes of the 329,387 corpus files and of the 7,646 compiler
test files do not change.

The repair is not specific to a language. A sum of error costs in 32 bits can become smaller than one of
its parts. A stack version then gets a cost that is less than the cost of one of its parts. The unmatched bracket
costs of patch 03 make the sums much larger, but a very large input with many errors also makes
the sum too large without patch 03.

Risk for upstream: low.

The patch applies to the upstream tag v0.27.0, after the patches with a smaller number. The
series compiles with `-Wall -Wextra` and no warning.

The comments hold the marker "(tree-sitter-cpp fork)". Remove the marker before you send the
patch upstream.

diff -ruN a/lib/src/error_costs.h b/lib/src/error_costs.h
--- a/lib/src/error_costs.h	2026-09-15 19:00:45.713044138 +0200
+++ b/lib/src/error_costs.h	2026-09-15 19:00:45.771517954 +0200
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 #ifndef TREE_SITTER_ERROR_COSTS_H_
 #define TREE_SITTER_ERROR_COSTS_H_
 
+#include <stdint.h>
+
 #define ERROR_STATE 0
 #define ERROR_COST_PER_RECOVERY 500
 #define ERROR_COST_PER_MISSING_TREE 110
@@ -18,4 +20,22 @@
 #define ERROR_COST_PER_UNMATCHED_BRACE 10000
 #define ERROR_COST_PER_UNMATCHED_PARENTHESIS 1000
 
+// The error costs of subtrees and of stack versions stop at ERROR_COST_MAX. A cost of ERROR_COST_MAX
+// tells that the full cost is ERROR_COST_MAX or more. A sum with a part of ERROR_COST_MAX is also
+// ERROR_COST_MAX, and two such costs are equal. The sums use 64 bits before they stop, and a sum
+// with no such part is exact. A sum of 32 bits can become smaller than one of its parts. An ERROR
+// node then gets a cost that is less than the cost of its unmatched brackets (tree-sitter-cpp fork).
+#define ERROR_COST_MAX UINT32_MAX
+
+// Stop a cost of 64 bits at ERROR_COST_MAX (tree-sitter-cpp fork).
+static inline uint32_t ts_error_cost_saturate(uint64_t cost) {
+  return cost >= ERROR_COST_MAX ? ERROR_COST_MAX : (uint32_t)cost;
+}
+
+// Add an increment to an error cost, and stop the sum at ERROR_COST_MAX. The increment must be
+// less than 2^63 (tree-sitter-cpp fork).
+static inline uint32_t ts_error_cost_add(uint32_t cost, uint64_t increment) {
+  return ts_error_cost_saturate((uint64_t)cost + increment);
+}
+
 #endif
